    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1366">

                <pb facs="1470" n="1456" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3431/76: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-24T12:00:00-04:00">April 24,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. Finance Minister<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1366-f1"/> assures me again that our
                    proposals for trade agreement will be accepted before he resigns office within
                    the next 2 or 3 weeks. He has induced the new Minister of Industry and <pb
                        facs="1471" n="1457" xml:id="pg1457"/> Commerce<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d1366-f2"/> to leave the matter in his (the Finance Minister’s)
                    hands. I had feared that the Minister of Industry and Commerce would insist upon
                    going into the entire problem anew.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
